        "type": "text",
        "text": "## Primary Request and Intent\n- Inspect `image-A.png` and `image-B.png` \"using only read_image, one tool call per response.\" Read A first; describe visible shape, color, and exact printed marker **before** requesting B; then describe B and compare.\n- Finish with a concise inspection record (~250 words) distinguishing directly observed facts from uncertainty, explaining how a reviewer can tell the items apart.\n- Constraints: \"Do not infer contents from filenames.\" \"Use exactly two read_image calls total, no other tools and no editing.\"\n- Follow-up: apply \"Reference 1\" (visual-evidence review standard) to the already-inspected images, \"do not read files again,\" producing a practical **300-word annotated checklist** with one finding per major section, flagging anything not supported by the images.\n- Required structure: observation + caveat sentences per item, evidence-class separation (direct observation / interpretation / unavailable), comparison table or parallel bullets in fixed field order, single identifiability conclusion, recommendations kept separate.\n\n## Key Technical Concepts\n- Tool `read_image` (path resolved by filesystem backend); PNG raster inspection only.\n- DSH file policy: read-only standing mode; approvals fail closed without an answerer.\n- Visual-evidence discipline: qualitative color names \u2260 colorimetry; no invented texture/lighting/vector history from rasters; transcriptions preserve letter case and digit order.\n- Matched pair design: identical canvas, background, label placement/typography; differing shape/color/text.\n\n## Files and Code\n- `/private/var/folders/jk/0kx3l0t93zj6gwlgth99c6lc0000gn/T/ds41f-step3br2-session-5n3m3jjo/workspace/image-A.png`: 384\u00d7384 PNG, 3460 bytes, sha256 begins `c1b1e6f9\u2026`; red circle, black marker `A17`.\n- `\u2026/workspace/image-B.png`: 384\u00d7384 PNG, 3073 bytes, sha256 begins `4cb99837\u2026`; blue square, black marker `B28`.\n- Normalized read-only copies under `\u2026/home/attachments/v1/objects/c1/\u2026` and `\u2026/4c/\u2026` (may be resized/re-encoded; source bytes may differ).\n- No files were created or edited.\n\n## Errors and Fixes"
